Subject: [PATCH] tests: setenv/unsetenv shim for Windows in test-llama-archs
 (block 11)

Block 11 hands the managed PLE reader budget to the load as
LLAMA_LAZY_BUF_MB, exported around llama_model_load with the POSIX
setenv/unsetenv. The MSVC CRT (which clang++ uses under the HIP SDK on
Windows) has neither, so a Windows build that includes the tests stops at
test-llama-archs.cpp. Map both onto _putenv_s under _WIN32: setenv keeps
the POSIX overwrite=0 semantics, and an empty value removes the variable.

No change on non-Windows builds.
---
 tests/test-llama-archs.cpp | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/test-llama-archs.cpp b/tests/test-llama-archs.cpp
index a98db39998..964ff4b942 100644
--- a/tests/test-llama-archs.cpp
+++ b/tests/test-llama-archs.cpp
@@ -24,6 +24,21 @@
 #include <utility>
 #include <vector>
 
+#ifdef _WIN32
+#include <cstdlib>
+
+// stew block 11 exports LLAMA_LAZY_BUF_MB with the POSIX calls; the MSVC CRT has only _putenv_s
+static int setenv(const char * name, const char * value, int overwrite) {
+    if (!overwrite && getenv(name) != nullptr) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    return _putenv_s(name, value);
+}
+static int unsetenv(const char * name) {
+    return _putenv_s(name, ""); // an empty value removes the variable
+}
+#endif
+
 static bool arch_matches(const std::string & filter, llm_arch arch) {
     if (filter.empty()) {
         return true;
